### Real-World Example 1: Claims Validation Extension Point

**Business Scenario**: State Medicaid agencies have unique claims validation rules that supplement federal requirements. State A requires specialized provider credentialing validation and service authorization checks.

**Core Product Extension Point Definition**:

```csharp
// Defined by core product
public interface IClaimsValidationExtension : IExtensionPoint<ClaimValidationContext, ValidationResult>
{
    Task<bool> AppliesAsync(ClaimValidationContext context);
}
```

**State A Implementation**:

```csharp
[Extension("claims.validation")]
public class StateAClaimsValidationExtension : IClaimsValidationExtension
{
    public string ExtensionPointId => "claims.validation";
    public Version InterfaceVersion => new Version(1, 0, 0);
    public int Priority => 150;

    public async Task<bool> AppliesAsync(ClaimValidationContext context)
    {
        return context.Claim.StateId == "StateA";
    }

    public async Task<ValidationResult> ExecuteAsync(
        ClaimValidationContext context,
        CancellationToken cancellationToken)
    {
        var errors = new List<ValidationError>();

        // State A Rule SA-001: Provider must be credentialed
        var provider = await _providerService.GetProviderAsync(context.Claim.ProviderId);
        if (provider == null || !provider.StateACredentialed)
        {
            errors.Add(new ValidationError
            {
                Code = "SA-001",
                Message = "Provider lacks State A credentialing"
            });
        }

        // State A Rule SA-002: Behavioral health requires prior authorization
        if (context.Claim.ServiceType == "BehavioralHealth")
        {
            var priorAuth = await _authService.CheckAuthorizationAsync(
                context.Claim.MemberId,
                context.Claim.ProcedureCode);

            if (!priorAuth.IsAuthorized)
            {
                errors.Add(new ValidationError
                {
                    Code = "SA-002",
                    Message = "Prior authorization required for behavioral health services"
                });
            }
        }

        return new ValidationResult
        {
            Success = !errors.Any(),
            Errors = errors
        };
    }
}
```

**Integration in Core Workflow**:

```csharp
public class ClaimsProcessingEngine
{
    public async Task<ClaimResult> ProcessClaimAsync(Claim claim)
    {
        // Standard validation (core)
        var coreValidation = await CoreValidationAsync(claim);
        if (!coreValidation.IsValid)
            return ClaimResult.Invalid(coreValidation.Errors);

        // Extension point: State-specific validation
        var extValidation = await _extensionExecutor.InvokeExtensionsAsync<
            ClaimValidationContext, ValidationResult>(
                "claims.validation",
                new ClaimValidationContext { Claim = claim });

        if (!extValidation.Success)
            return ClaimResult.Invalid(extValidation.Errors);

        // Continue adjudication
        return await AdjudicateClaimAsync(claim);
    }
}
```

**Benefits**:
- State A validation rules isolated in separate assembly
- Core product unchanged when State A updates rules
- Other states unaffected by State A changes
- Extension can be tested independently

